---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { OFFLINE_AI } from '../../../../courses/offline-ai/syllabus';
import '../../../../styles/math.css';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
---
<CourseHome course={OFFLINE_AI}>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>What you will have at the end</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A private assistant</strong> that runs on your own laptop or desktop with the internet switched off.</li>
      <li><strong>Search across your own documents</strong>: ask questions of your PDFs and notes and get answers with the page they came from.</li>
      <li><strong>Your own workflows</strong>: small Python programs that send work to the model on your machine, such as summarising a folder of files every night.</li>
      <li><strong>A cost sheet</strong> comparing your setup with Claude, ChatGPT and Google plans, in rupees, Canadian dollars, US dollars or pounds.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Want to know how the model works inside, with the maths? The free course <a href="/learn/courses/ml-foundations/">From a straight line to an LLM</a> builds up from linear regression to attention and transformers, with a simulation in every lesson.</p>
  </section>
  <p class="cs-meta"><strong>Quick reference:</strong> <a href="/learn/courses/offline-ai/glossary/">glossary of terms</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/offline-ai/cheat-sheet/">cheat sheet of commands</a></p>
</CourseHome>
